Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and how they will be used  

• "alternate_bases": detect how many alternate alleles a variant has (keep only variants with ARRAY_SIZE("alternate_bases") = 1).  
• "call": nested array that stores one object per sample. We FLATTEN it to reach every sample’s genotype.  
    – value:"name": the sample‑ID we will group by.  
    – value:"genotype"[0] and value:"genotype"[1]: the two allele codes; we keep records where both = 0 (homozygous reference).  
• "Sample" (in _1000_GENOMES_SAMPLE_INFO): optional for joining population metadata.  

Main filter conditions  

1. ARRAY_SIZE(v."alternate_bases") = 1   -- exactly one ALT allele  
2. f.value:"genotype"[0]::NUMBER = 0  
3. f.value:"genotype"[1]::NUMBER = 0       -- hom‑ref (0/0)  

Below are ten progressively richer Snowflake queries (all capped with LIMIT 20 for previewing) that explore the data and finish with the query that returns the desired ranking.  

```sql
--Query 1 – Description: quick look at raw rows in the phase‑3 variants table.
SELECT *
FROM "HUMAN_GENOME_VARIANTS"."HUMAN_GENOME_VARIANTS"."_1000_GENOMES_PHASE_3_VARIANTS_20150220"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Query 2 – Description: inspect the structure of one “call” object after flattening.
SELECT v."reference_name",
       v."start_position",
       f.value AS "call_object"
FROM "HUMAN_GENOME_VARIANTS"."HUMAN_GENOME_VARIANTS"."_1000_GENOMES_PHASE_3_VARIANTS_20150220" v,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => v."call") f
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Query 3 – Description: pull sample names and their two genotype alleles.
SELECT f.value:"name"::STRING        AS "sample_name",
       f.value:"genotype"[0]::NUMBER AS "allele_1",
       f.value:"genotype"[1]::NUMBER AS "allele_2"
FROM "HUMAN_GENOME_VARIANTS"."HUMAN_GENOME_VARIANTS"."_1000_GENOMES_PHASE_3_VARIANTS_20150220" v,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => v."call") f
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Query 4 – Description: see how many alternate alleles each variant possesses.
SELECT v."reference_name",
       v."start_position",
       ARRAY_SIZE(v."alternate_bases") AS "alt_count"
FROM "HUMAN_GENOME_VARIANTS"."HUMAN_GENOME_VARIANTS"."_1000_GENOMES_PHASE_3_VARIANTS_20150220" v
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Query 5 – Description: list variants that have exactly one alternate allele.
SELECT v."reference_name",
       v."start_position",
       ARRAY_SIZE(v."alternate_bases") AS "alt_count"
FROM "HUMAN_GENOME_VARIANTS"."HUMAN_GENOME_VARIANTS"."_1000_GENOMES_PHASE_3_VARIANTS_20150220" v
WHERE ARRAY_SIZE(v."alternate_bases") = 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Query 6 – Description: obtain sample calls that are homozygous reference (0/0) for single‑ALT variants.
SELECT f.value:"name"::STRING AS "sample_name",
       v."reference_name",
       v."start_position"
FROM "HUMAN_GENOME_VARIANTS"."HUMAN_GENOME_VARIANTS"."_1000_GENOMES_PHASE_3_VARIANTS_20150220" v,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => v."call") f
WHERE ARRAY_SIZE(v."alternate_bases") = 1
  AND f.value:"genotype"[0]::NUMBER = 0
  AND f.value:"genotype"[1]::NUMBER = 0
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Query 7 – Description: count the number of such homozygous reference positions per sample (first 20 rows).
SELECT f.value:"name"::STRING               AS "sample_name",
       COUNT(*)                             AS "hom_ref_positions"
FROM "HUMAN_GENOME_VARIANTS"."HUMAN_GENOME_VARIANTS"."_1000_GENOMES_PHASE_3_VARIANTS_20150220" v,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => v."call") f
WHERE ARRAY_SIZE(v."alternate_bases") = 1
  AND f.value:"genotype"[0]::NUMBER = 0
  AND f.value:"genotype"[1]::NUMBER = 0
GROUP BY f.value:"name"::STRING
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Query 8 – Description: same as Q7 but ordered to show the highest counts first.
SELECT f.value:"name"::STRING               AS "sample_name",
       COUNT(*)                             AS "hom_ref_positions"
FROM "HUMAN_GENOME_VARIANTS"."HUMAN_GENOME_VARIANTS"."_1000_GENOMES_PHASE_3_VARIANTS_20150220" v,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => v."call") f
WHERE ARRAY_SIZE(v."alternate_bases") = 1
  AND f.value:"genotype"[0]::NUMBER = 0
  AND f.value:"genotype"[1]::NUMBER = 0
GROUP BY f.value:"name"::STRING
ORDER BY "hom_ref_positions" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Query 9 – Description: attach population metadata from the sample‑info table.
WITH hom_ref AS (
    SELECT f.value:"name"::STRING AS "sample_name",
           COUNT(*)               AS "hom_ref_positions"
    FROM "HUMAN_GENOME_VARIANTS"."HUMAN_GENOME_VARIANTS"."_1000_GENOMES_PHASE_3_VARIANTS_20150220" v,
         LATERAL FLATTEN(input => v."call") f
    WHERE ARRAY_SIZE(v."alternate_bases") = 1
      AND f.value:"genotype"[0]::NUMBER = 0
      AND f.value:"genotype"[1]::NUMBER = 0
    GROUP BY f.value:"name"::STRING
)
SELECT h."sample_name",
       h."hom_ref_positions",
       s."Population",
       s."Super_Population"
FROM hom_ref h
LEFT JOIN "HUMAN_GENOME_VARIANTS"."HUMAN_GENOME_VARIANTS"."_1000_GENOMES_SAMPLE_INFO" s
       ON s."Sample" = h."sample_name"
ORDER BY h."hom_ref_positions" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Query 10 – Description: final statement returning the (up to) top‑10 samples
--                     having the largest count of homozygous reference calls
--                     on loci with exactly one alternate allele.
SELECT f.value:"name"::STRING               AS "sample_name",
       COUNT(*)                             AS "hom_ref_positions"
FROM "HUMAN_GENOME_VARIANTS"."HUMAN_GENOME_VARIANTS"."_1000_GENOMES_PHASE_3_VARIANTS_20150220" v,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => v."call") f
WHERE ARRAY_SIZE(v."alternate_bases") = 1
  AND f.value:"genotype"[0]::NUMBER = 0
  AND f.value:"genotype"[1]::NUMBER = 0
GROUP BY f.value:"name"::STRING
ORDER BY "hom_ref_positions" DESC
LIMIT 20;   -- the first 10 rows of this result set answer the task
```
